dmw - dwm made in wayland
=========================

dmw ports dwm to suckless Wayland. It uses neuswc for window management and
neuwld to draw the bar. This is a bit more "feature"-full thanks to the extra
neuswc/neuwld patches from MICE (a seperate project).

See: my forks of neuswc/neuwld which apply these patches that haven't been
upstreamed yet (most of the patches come from xplshn):

- https://git.daat.foo/neuswc/file/README.html
- https://git.daat.foo/neuwld/file/README.html

Disclaimer
----------

Unlike other neuswc/neuwld compositors, this is targeted against an
experimental in production version of neuswc which applies (and will continue
to apply) many patches that are not within the main neuswc/neuwld project (yet).
While it's not as unstable or as breaking as wlroots (in fact these APIs only
add more compatibility and fixes on top of neuswc), it can be frustrating because
dmw will always reflect these new changes (or at least if it's applicable).

These patches are tested before they are published on my repos, and in fact, 
there are still many more to come since MICE is a relatively old project that
has been in development for a long time now (ever since aruu was created).

Before you pull the latest commits of dmw, please check the commit messages
and be sure to also check the neuswc/neuwld for any new changes.

Here be dragons.

Build
-----

Install neuswc and neuwld with the MICE port patches, their pkg-config
files (swc.pc and wld.pc), and wayland-scanner. The build reads swc.xml
from the installed neuswc prefix. For a static-only neuswc installation
use make PKG_CONFIG='pkg-config --static'.

    make
    make install

The first build copies config.def.h to config.h. Edit config.h and rebuild
to change bindings, colors, fonts or rules. Rules match substrings of the
Wayland app ID and title. The default commands are `st-wl` and `neumenu_run`.

Run
---

From a VT with XDG_RUNTIME_DIR set, run:

    swc-launch dmw

Inside an existing Wayland session, use the nested backend:

    SWC_BACKEND=nested dmw

Alt-Shift-Return starts a terminal. Alt-p opens the launcher.
Alt-Shift-q exits. See config.h if you want to change the default MOD key.

The bar reads one status line at a time from stdin:

    while date; do sleep 1; done | swc-launch dmw

Patches
-------

This project tries to not overstep it's boundaries with what a tiling wm
should do and implement just like the original dwm. It should be relatively
easy to patch dmw.

Patches live in https://git.daat.foo/dmw-patches/log.html. See Contributing
below if you would like to contribute to the repository of patches or this
project in particular.

Contributing
------------

All development is on the [stagit repo](https://git.daat.foo/dmw/log.html).
However while it is much preferred, you can send PRs in the github mirror.
It's just frowned upon (my me). All contributions should be sent via email.

Run a quick `git format-patch HEAD~1` and send to *cowmonk@based.pt* with the 
subject head of `[PATCH] dmw`. Consider reading the manpages of `git-send-email`
if you are interested in moving towards email for development.

I *strongly* suggest pgp encrypting your email, in which case my public keys
can be found on `keys.openpgp.org` or here:

